Toyshop
Who knows what might be hidden in the dark rafters and shadowy corners of this emporium?

There's a closed oak chest in the northeast corner.

A young woman stands attentively nearby.

>wait
Time passes.

"Welcome," says the young woman, "My father usually runs the store, but I'm afraid he isn't here today and I'm looking after the store. My name is Catharine."

>wait
Time passes.

Catharine opens the chest and roots around inside it. "I wonder if your niece would like something like this?" she says. "It's quite old, but I think it still works." She closes the chest and shows you a small cardboard box. She holds it up to her ear and shakes it. "Sounds like it's all there. It does require some assembly, though," she adds, and hands the box to you.

[Your score has just gone up by one point.]

