>examine sundial
You're not quite sure why you never noticed the sundial before. It's a square pedestal of stone, with markings for the hours. The gnomon casts a shadow over the flat surface.

>put mushroom in shadow
You place the mushroom on the sundial. As the tip of the shadow falls across the mushroom, a white door appears in the mushroom's stalk. An inch-high man in shorts and t-shirt walks through the door and stares up at you, aghast, before turning on his heels and exiting through the door, which vanishes as soon as it closes. He left something behind, though.

>examine sundial
You're not quite sure why you never noticed the sundial before. It's a square pedestal of stone, with markings for the hours. The gnomon casts a shadow over the flat surface. On the sundial are a featureless mahogany rod and a mushroom.

>take rod
Taken.

>strike rod
The rod charges with etherial power, drawn up from the earth through ley lines...

>point rod at egg
A tiny gout of fire leaps out from the tip of the rod, neatly cooking the egg, which is now too hot to hold, and you drop it.

